{"version": 1, "sourceSha256": "a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9756359479faafff5ce16cc3aed21e5c570fe4a1b58bf", "documents": [{"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, {"id": "offline-a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9", "filename": "6-Part C.mp3", "sha256": "a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9756359479faafff5ce16cc3aed21e5c570fe4a1b58bf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-5/a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9756359479faafff5ce16cc3aed21e5c570fe4a1b58bf.mp3", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9756359479faafff5ce16cc3aed21e5c570fe4a1b58bf.json", "format": "mp3", "role": "recording"}], "units": [{"id": "jahshan-1QBPaJWBxa1M80nhpspfjppe0T6V_x018-C-0", "label": "Jahshan set 6 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "pages": [83, 84, 85, 86], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "Dr Marsh says that one aim of the new guidelines on concussion is\nA. to educate young sportspeople in how to avoid getting it.\nB. to correct some common misunderstandings about it.\nC. to provide a range of specialist advice about it.", "sourcePage": 83, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "Dr Marsh makes the point that someone who has suffered a concussion will\nA. be unconscious for varying amounts of time after the event.\nB. need a medical examination before doing any further exercise.\nC. have to take precautions to avoid the risk of symptoms recurring.", "sourcePage": 83, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "Dr Marsh says returning to sport too early after a concussion is dangerous\nbecause\nA. a subsequent episode can have a cumulative effect.\nB. there is a high risk of fatality in the event of a second one.\nC. the brains of younger people need time to return to normal size.", "sourcePage": 83, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "Dr Marsh suggests that the risk of sustaining a concussion in sports\nA. lies mainly in the choice of sports played.\nB. can be reduced by developing good playing technique.\nC. is greater when sports are played in less formal situations.", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "What is Dr Marsh's view about providing medical support for youth sports\nevents?\nA. Some types of sport are risky enough to justify it.\nB. The organisers should be capable of dealing with any issues.\nC. Certain medical professionals should be encouraged to volunteer.", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Dr Marsh thinks that developments in college football in the USA\nA. only really address an issue which is particular to that sport.\nB. are only likely to benefit the health of professional sports players.\nC. are a significant step forward in the prevention of concussion in all sports.\nNow look at extract two.\n\nExtract 2: Questions 37-42\nYou hear a presentation by a consultant cardiologist called Dr Pamela Skelton, who's talking\nabout a research trial called SPRINT which investigated the effects of setting lower blood-\npressure targets.\nYou now have 90 seconds to read questions 37-42.", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "Why was the SPRINT trial stopped before it was due to end?\nA. There were conclusive results earlier than expected.\nB. The high drop-out rate was likely to invalidate the data.\nC. Concerns were raised about possible effects on all participants.", "sourcePage": 85, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "A few participants aged over seventy-five left the trial because\nA. there was a negative impact on their daily life.\nB. they failed to take the required doses of medication.\nC. their health deteriorated due to pre-existing conditions.", "sourcePage": 85, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "A significant feature of measuring blood pressure in the trial was that\nA. the highest of three readings was recorded.\nB. the patient was alone when it was carried out.\nC. it was done manually by the participant at home.", "sourcePage": 85, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "How did the SPRINT trial differ from the earlier ACCORD study into blood pressure?\nA. SPRINT had fewer participants.\nB. SPRINT involved higher-risk patients.\nC. SPRINT included patients with diabetes.", "sourcePage": 86, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "Dr Skelton's main reservation about the SPRINT trial is that\nA. it ignores the wider implications of lowered BP.\nB. its results go against the existing body of evidence.\nC. it was unduly influenced by pharmaceutical companies.", "sourcePage": 86, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "What impact does Dr Skelton think the SPRINT trial will have in the future?\nA. It will lead to universally applicable guidelines for BP levels.\nB. Increased attention will be given to the effect of lifestyle on BP.\nC. GPs will adopt a more active approach to lowering BP in the elderly.\nYou now have two minutes to check your answers.\nEND OF THE LISTENING TEST", "sourcePage": 86, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 89, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["a2d9cc39e598a8c2acc9756359479faafff5ce16cc3aed21e5c570fe4a1b58bf"], "answerSources": [], "matchEvidence": "Exact original recording SHA-256 in the verified Jahshan collection"}]}
